===Etymology===
Coined by {{w|William Shakespeare}} in ''[[:w:Anthony and Cleopatra|Anthony and Cleopatra]]'' around 1607.<ref>{{cite-book|author=Albert Jack|year=2005|title=Red herrings and white elephants|publisher=HarperCollins|page= 44|pageurl=http://books.google.co.jp/books?id=NSMq-PhYVq4C&pg=PA44|ISBN=978-0-06-084337-3|passage=The phrase is a simple one with a simple origin provided, once again, by Shakespeare.}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun|head=[[salad]] [[day]]s}}

# A [[period]] of [[inexperienced]] [[youthful]] [[innocence]] accompanied by [[enthusiasm]] and [[idealism]].
#* '''1623''', {{w|William Shakespeare}}, ''[[:w:Anthony and Cleopatra|The Tragedie of Antonie and Cleopatra]]'' in ''[https://archive.org/details/mrvvilliamshakes00shak/page/n8/mode/1up Mr William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies...'', [https://archive.org/details/mrvvilliamshakes00shak/page/344/mode/1up Act I, Scene v]:
#*: ''[[Cleopatra|Cleo.]]'' Did I ''Charmian'', [[ever|euer]] [[love|loue]] ''Caesar'' [[so|ſo]]? ... My '''[[salad|Sallad]] [[days|dayes]]''',<br>When I was [[green]]e in [[judgment|iudgment]], cold in blood...
#* {{quote-journal|en|month=October|year=1874|work=The American Educational Monthly|chapter=Salad Days|page=462|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=QLPgypwGPF0C&pg=PA462&dq=%22salad+days%22&hl=&cd=18&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22salad%20days%22&f=false|passage=The season of '''salad days''' has been rightly called a season of folly—rightly, because nature wisely intended '''salad days''' for folly, and we are wise to regard them as a time for folly. But are we wise when, halting upon the crutches age finds convenient after the gambols of youth have lost their attractions, we condemn this season of harmless folly to perpetual reprobation?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/1952/05/i-like-to-be-a-stranger/640931/|title=I Like to Be a Stranger|year=1952|month=May|author=George Santayana|authorlink=George Santayana|work=The Atlantic|passage=But it must be in solitude. I do not need or desire to hobnob artificially with other old men in order to revisit them in their '''salad days''', and to renew my own.}}
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=XX|passage=“I'll bet he was swiping things as a small boy.” “Only biscuits.” “I beg your pardon?” “Or crackers you would call them, wouldn't you? He was telling me he occasionally pinched a cracker or two in his '''salad days'''.”}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2015|actor=Timothy Dalton|role=Sir Malcolm Murray|title=Penny Dreadful|season=2|number=6|time=23m30s|passage=Do you know I've not been to a ball in ages? I used to be quite the dancer in my '''salad days''', if you can believe such a thing.}}
#* '''2023''' Feb. 24, Annie Mebane, ''[[:w:Shrinking (TV series)|Shrinking]]'', Season 1, Episode 6: 
#*: ''Liz:'' Derek, remember when I used to want to fuck all the time?<br>''Derek:'' Ah, yes. The '''salad days'''.<br>''Liz:'' Mmh. Now, my sex window is between 3 and 3:20 pm and Derek needs ''not'' to have annoyed me that day.<br>''Derek:'' Doesn't happen often.

